# One Juku E5101/E5104 386K CP/M volume: 80 tracks on one side, 10 physical
# 512-byte sectors per track.  The zero-based skew table is the physical-sector
# grouping produced by the BIOS's 40-entry 128-byte record translation table.
# arch/juku/mksides.py converts this flat volume to the machine's cylinder/head
# interleaved 800K raw-image container.
diskdef juku386
    seclen 512
    tracks 80
    sectrk 10
    blocksize 2048
    maxdir 128
    boottrk 2
    skewtab 0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9
    os 2.2
end


